EXT. THE MOSSBACK FERRY - ENCHANTED MARSH - TWILIGHT

A flat-bottomed barge poled across a lake of black glass. Willow roots hang down like grey hair. Lanterns made of glass beetles bob at the corners of the deck. Frogs sing in a low, ancient chord.

ORLAITH, 20s, a young ranger in moss-green leathers, leans on the rail with a longbow slung behind her shoulder. Freckles. Sharp grin. She watches the water for movement.

THORNE, 40s, her older brother, stands at the prow, hand on his sword hilt, jaw set against a wind that isn't there. Broad. Scarred. Silent as a post.

BRACKEN, 60s, the ferryman, poles the barge with slow, patient strokes. A bent old man in a coat sewn from bark and feathers. One eye milky white.

MISTRESS YARROW, 50s, a herbalist in a patched purple cloak, kneels on the deck sorting dried flowers into a wooden case. She hums.

PIPKIN THE LESS, 12, a boy no taller than a barrel, hides behind a stack of crates and clutches a talking lantern, which whispers to him.

ORLAITH
How long till the far bank, Bracken?

BRACKEN
Long as it takes.

ORLAITH
That's not an answer.

BRACKEN
It's the only one.

She rolls her eyes, but her grin deepens. Thorne glances back at his sister, then forward again. Yarrow lifts a flower to the light.

YARROW
Moonthistle. Almost gone from the marsh.

ORLAITH
You've got a whole case.

YARROW
That's why it's almost gone.

PIPKIN
(whispering to the lantern)
She's stealing it.

LANTERN
(a tiny voice)
Not stealing. Gathering.

PIPKIN
Same thing.

THORNE
Pipkin.

PIPKIN
Yes, Thorne?

THORNE
Stop talking to the lantern.

PIPKIN
He talks first.

THORNE
Then stop answering.

Pipkin sulks. The ferry glides through a curtain of willow, and the light changes to a deep underwater green. Everyone falls quiet. Even the frogs.

BRACKEN
Hush now.

ORLAITH
What is it?

BRACKEN
Something old.

Thorne draws his sword an inch. Orlaith slips an arrow from her quiver without taking her eyes off the water. Yarrow closes the case with a quiet click. Pipkin ducks lower, and the lantern's glow dims to the colour of a candle in a drawer.

The water bulges, slow and enormous, then settles again, leaving nothing but a ring of ripples spreading toward the banks.

BRACKEN (CONT'D)
(softly)
Gone.

THORNE
What was that?

BRACKEN
The marsh saying hello.

ORLAITH
(muttering)
Friendly.

YARROW
It means we're welcome.

PIPKIN
(peeping out)
Can I come out now?

BRACKEN
Aye, boy.

Pipkin scrambles out from behind the crates. He sits beside Yarrow, who gives him a sprig of moonthistle without a word. He tucks it behind his ear, grinning.

The ferry drifts into the open water once more, and up ahead, through the gathering dusk, the far bank shimmers like a lit window.
